finding: Medium — run-level signals can be lost during post-child finalization, yielding a green run. `bun /tmp/shallot-review-final-signal-probe.ts` emitted `signalSent:true`, `summarySeenBeforeSignal:false`, and `exitCode:0`; the runner then printed `1 passed, 0 failed` and kept the Bun JUnit report at `failures="0"`. The probe waited until the child TMP directory was removed, then sent SIGTERM while 80 MB of captured output kept synchronous artifact writing in progress. `RunSignals` is asynchronous, but finalization closes handlers and calls `process.exit` without yielding/checking pending signals. A boundary probe sent SIGTERM immediately after the first row's temp cleanup; it launched the next `bun test` child, which was interrupted before the check body, and reported that row as failed (so no later check body ran, and that red was counted). The finalization false-green is the finding.
